1 NOTE 1927- Children and relatives of Mrs. Ragnhild Bjorgo assembled at her home on Sunday July 10th to help her celebrate her 70th birthday.  She was seventy years old on Thursday July 14, but to accommodate those unable to be present 
2 CONC on that day the other date was chosen for the occasion.  Mrs. Bjorgo who is the widow of Gunelius Bjorgo, enjoyed a day with fifty-two relatives, including her children.  Only three of her seventeen grandchildren weren't there: Be
2 CONC nora Lee, La Crosse and Bernice and Vernon of Austin, Minnesota.
2 CONT
2 CONT When she died at her home on Feb 27, 1938 she had twenty granchildren, and nine great-granchildren.  Her sister Mrs. Julia Ellingson, of Kendallville, Iowa.  Three other sisters and a brother have died.  Her funeral was held on Ma
2 CONC rch 3, 1938.  She had enjoyed good health until a week before her death.  She had spent her entire life in Highland township.  She was baptized by Rev. Clauson and confirmed by Rev. H. A. Stub in the Big Canoe church.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was a pleasant and agreeable person which manner gained for her the respect of all with whom she came in contact.  The entire community and especially the Tabitha Ladies' Aid have lost a true and faithful member and she will b
2 CONC e sadly missed.  She was a charter member of the Highland and Tabitha Ladies' Aids.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her pallbearers were six grandsons:  Myron and Truman Peterson, Roman, Lloyd and Gordon Bjorgo and Roman Lee.
1 CHAN
2 DATE 27 OCT 2017
3 TIME 04:15:40
