1 NOTE
2 CONT November 22, 1962 - Funeral Rites Held November 3, for Elias L. Bjorgo - Elias L. Bjorgo, son of Gunerious and Ragnhild Bjorgo, was born September 20, 1881 in Highland Township.  He passed away at the Spring Grove Hospital on Nove
2 CONC mber 1, 1962 after a lingering illness at the age of 81 years, 1 month and 11 days.  He was baptized and confirmed at Big Canoe by Pastor Seehus.  He spent his entire life in this community where he attended the rural schools and 
2 CONC was engaged in farming until he retired 9 years ago.  On September 15, 1910 he was united in marriage to Julia Halverson at the Waterloo Ridge Church by Pastor Wilhelmson.  He is survived by his wife and three sons:  Gilmen of Hig
2 CONC hland Township; Roman of Charles City, IA and Lloyd, also of Highland Township with whom he made his home since retiring.  He is also survived by one brother, Henry of Austin, MN and several nieces and nephews.  He was preceded in
2 CONC  death by his parents, two brothers and four sisters.  One brother died in infancy.
2 CONT Funeral services were held November 3, 1962 at the Big Canoe Church with Pastor Hexom officiating.  Mrs. Hexom was the organist and Mrs. Earl Arneson the soloist.
2 CONT Honorary pallbearers were:  Jens Shuros, Gust Sacaquitne, Selmer Strinmoen, Selmer Askelson, John Norgard, Arthur Shuros, Myer Sacquitne, Benard Strinmoen, Bernard Shuros and Oren Anderson.  Casket bearers were:  Gordon Bjorgo, Ve
2 CONC rnon Bjorgo, Myron Peterson, David Peterson, Leonard Lane and Carlton Clauson.
2 CONT
2 CONT September 29, 1904 - Mrs. Arne Lee of Mabel, MN was here Friday to see her brother, Elias Bjorgo, who was the victim of a serious accident recently in which he had his eye injured by the pointed end of a file.
2 CONT
2 CONT March 26, 1908 - Elias and Albert Bjorgo will conduct the John Gaare farm this year.  They will also run a cream route and two other farms in connection.
1 NOTE
2 CONT Attendants for their wedding were:  Emma Bjorgo Peterson, Marie Evenmoe Raaen, Martin Bjorgo, Gilma Lee, Maren and Genora Overhaug Horgen, the two latter were flower girls.  Alice Hanson Thompson and Myer Wevley were also attendan
2 CONC ts but were unable to be present.  Olai Langlie deceased, was also an attendant.
